      },
      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The complete vav descends into one broad oval-to-horizontal foot fused to the stem. No independent top edge distinguishes a swollen point from a transverse bar, paired dots, or an ordinary terminal with surrounding ink. Literal mem patah in לְמַעֲשֵׂי, lamed tsere in לֵב, first-lamed qamats in אֻמְלָלִים, and the same-row lower outlines in רָאִיתִי and יוֹדֵעַ expose their competing geometries. The target lacks sufficient separately delimited structure to select a vowel or certify absence. Retain the disclosure.",
      "physicalLocator": {
        "id": "bel-1-35-246-vayomer35-letter1-vowel",
        "anchorScalarSpan": [
          0,
          7
        ],
        "targetScalarIndex": 0,
        "targetClusterScalarSpan": [
          0,
          1
        ],
        "targetClusterScalars": [
          "U+05D5"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "note": {
        "id": "bel-1-35-246-vayomer35-letter2-dagesh",
        "kind": "unreadablePoint",
        "anchor": "ויֹאמֶר",
        "occurrence": 1,
        "letterIndex": 2,
        "mark": "dagesh",
        "sourcePages": [
          246
        ],
        "sourceURL": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikisource/he/e/ed/Apocrypha_Kahana_A2.pdf#page=246"
      },
      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The yod beneath its retained holam has a shallow left inset and a thick continuous lower body. The first yod in source36 ויציגהו exposes a separate round interior dagesh below the head with white separation; same-row ordinary yods in רָאִיתִי, יְיָ and יוֹדֵעַ show variable head widths and descending tails. The target has no securely bounded round side node and remains compatible with a heavy ordinary yod or obscured dagesh. Preserve holam and the disclosure.",
      "physicalLocator": {
        "id": "bel-1-35-246-vayomer35-letter2-dagesh",
        "anchorScalarSpan": [
          0,
          7
        ],
        "targetScalarIndex": 1,
